Globally Harmonized System of Classification and Labelling of Chemicals — UN (@cs-ghs: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_3JK41Y6PYJ4063TNSBZ6ZJ50PG
United Nations. Globally Harmonized System of Classification and Labelling of Chemicals, eleventh revised edition, September 2025. [Official book](https://unece.org/info/Transport/pub/407575) · [UN explanation and revision context](https://unece.org/about-ghs).

Read the book's introductory framework, the complete relevant physical/health/environmental hazard chapters and communication annexes. In advanced classification work read the full volume and its cited evidence. Distinguish hazard criteria, supplier safety information, a product specification and transport classification.

The official edition and free consultation status were checked on 29 October 2026. UN reproduction/translation permissions apply; free reading is not unrestricted reuse. GHS revisions and national adoption can differ. The reading develops the ability to interpret source evidence and identify the applicable edition, without treating a historical label or simplified diagram as a complete current substance assessment. No source file is bundled.

